      {
        "id": 52686,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-29T03:51:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Given the sequence \"Start of the Environment Turn,\" \"Play an Environment Card,\" \"End of the Environment Turn,\"&nbsp;assuming that you played the environment card as normally during it's turn, you will have already passed the start of the environment turn.&nbsp; The effect will not occur until the next upcoming \"Start of the Environment Turn.\"&nbsp; Had it been played as the effect of another \"at the start of the environment turn\" effect, then it would still be the start of the environment turn and would act immediately.</p><p>On the back of the rule book it explains the round, turns of the round, and phases of the turns, if you need the reference.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:26:39.382Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
