        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Given the sequence &quot;Start of the Environment Turn,&quot; &quot;Play an Environment Card,&quot; &quot;End of the Environment Turn,&quot;&nbsp;assuming that you played the environment card as normally during it&#39;s turn, you will have already passed the start of the environment turn.&nbsp; The effect will not occur until the next upcoming &quot;Start of the Environment Turn.&quot;&nbsp; Had it been played as the effect of another &quot;at the start of the environment turn&quot; effect, then it would still be the start of the environment turn and would act immediately.</p><p>On the back of the rule book it explains the round, turns of the round, and phases of the turns, if you need the reference.</p>",
